OBP hang: guard find-child-device against a child with no "reg".

md-iodevice-props.fth's find-child-device reads each PCI child's "reg" with an
unconditional drop after get-package-property. A child with no "reg" makes that
drop eat the phandle, and the sibling walk then runs off into garbage -- OBP
hangs before its banner. Check the flag instead: no "reg" just means not a
match, keep walking.

This is what lets the stand-init "pci-network" branch (which stamps a per-NIC
local-mac-address from the MD) run on QEMU's flat PCIe bus, where a real
T2000's deep switch tree is not there to keep the walk short. Build-tree only,
never src/obp.

--- a/obp/arch/sun4v/md-iodevice-props.fth
+++ b/obp/arch/sun4v/md-iodevice-props.fth
@@ -121,10 +121,13 @@
    child dup if						( dev fcn phandle )
       begin						( dev fcn phandle )
          dup if						( dev fcn phandle )
-            dup " reg" rot get-package-property drop	( dev fcn phandle reg,len )
-            decode-int nip nip				( dev fcn phandle phys.hi )
-            2over rot					( dev fcn phandle dev fcn phys.hi )
-            tuck cfg>fcn# = -rot cfg>dev# = and 0=	( dev fcn phandle flag )
+            dup " reg" rot get-package-property if	( dev fcn phandle )
+               true				\ no "reg" on this child: not a match, keep walking
+            else					( dev fcn phandle reg,len )
+               decode-int nip nip			( dev fcn phandle phys.hi )
+               2over rot				( dev fcn phandle dev fcn phys.hi )
+               tuck cfg>fcn# = -rot cfg>dev# = and 0=	( dev fcn phandle flag )
+            then					( dev fcn phandle flag )
          else						( dev fcn phandle )
             false					( dev fcn phandle flag )
          then						( dev fcn phandle )
